 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "affect/effect · lose/loose · economic/economical · beside/besides",
   "en": "affect and effect · lose and loose · economic and economical · beside and besides"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "철자와 발음이 비슷해 헷갈리는 단어는 품사로 구별합니다. affect는 동사(영향을 미치다), effect는 명사(영향, 효과)입니다. lose /luːz/는 동사(잃다), loose /luːs/는 형용사(헐렁한)입니다. economic은 경제의(economic growth), economical은 경제적인/절약하는(an economical car)입니다. beside는 ~ 옆에, besides는 게다가/~ 외에입니다. advice는 명사(조언, 셀 수 없음), advise는 동사(조언하다)입니다. 같은 어근이어도 철자 하나로 뜻과 품사가 바뀌므로 짝으로 외웁니다.",
   "en": "Words with similar spelling or sound are separated by word class. Affect is a verb (to influence); effect is a noun (result). Lose is a verb (to fail to keep); loose is an adjective (not tight). Economic means relating to the economy (economic growth); economical means cheap to run (an economical car). Beside means next to; besides means in addition. Advice is an uncountable noun; advise is a verb. Learn them as pairs because one letter changes the meaning and word class."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "단어 / Word",
    "품사 / Class",
    "예문 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "affect / effect",
     "verb / noun",
     "It affects me. It has an effect."
    ],
    [
     "lose / loose",
     "verb / adjective",
     "Don't lose it. It's loose."
    ],
    [
     "economic / economical",
     "adj / adj",
     "economic growth / an economical car"
    ],
    [
     "advice / advise",
     "noun / verb",
     "Take my advice. I advise you to wait."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "affect는 동사, effect는 명사입니다. 예외로 effect는 ‘초래하다’는 동사로도 쓰입니다.",
    "en": "Effect can rarely be a verb meaning to bring about."
   },
   {
    "ko": "advice는 셀 수 없는 명사입니다. an advice(×)",
    "en": "Advice is uncountable: not an advice."
   },
   {
    "ko": "beside와 besides는 의미가 완전히 다릅니다.",
    "en": "Beside and besides have different meanings."
   }
